%N A399187 The determinant of an n X n matrix formed by placing the first n^2 primes in L-shaped gnomons in alternating directions.
%H A399187 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A399187/b399187.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..292</a>
%H A399187 Nicolay Avilov, <a href="/A399187/a399187.jpg">Illustration of a(1)..a(5)</a>
%e A399187          |  2----3   23---29   97 |
%e A399187          |       |    |    |    | |
%e A399187          |  7----5   19   31   89 |
%e A399187          |  |         |    |    | |
%e A399187   a(5) = | 11---13---17   37   83 | = 5917632.
%e A399187          |                 |    | |
%e A399187          | 53---47---43---41   79 |
%e A399187          |  |                   | |
%e A399187          | 59---61---67---71---73 |
%p A399187 a:= n-> LinearAlgebra[Determinant](Matrix(n, (i, j)->
%p A399187    (t-> ithprime(1+t*(t-1)+(i-j)*(-1)^t))(max(i, j)))):
%p A399187 seq(a(n), n=0..15);  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Aug 24 2026
%o A399187 (PARI)
%o A399187 Mtx(n) = matrix(n,n,i,j, my(t=max(i,j)); 1 + t*(t-1) + (-1)^t*(i-j))
%o A399187 a(n) = matdet(apply(prime, Mtx(n))) \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 24 2026, after _Alois P. Heinz_
